WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.512
Security operations use OT telemetry in several ways.

00:00:04.512 --> 00:00:09.025
Detection engineering turns known conditions into maintained alerts.

00:00:09.025 --> 00:00:13.537
Threat hunting asks focused questions across historical data.

00:00:13.537 --> 00:00:22.800
Anomaly detection identifies deviation from expected behavior, while incident response reconstructs identities, assets, communication, changes, and process impact.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.837
The same telemetry can update asset inventory.

00:00:26.837 --> 00:00:36.574
Newly observed devices, changed peers, dormant systems returning to service, and unexpected protocols should be validated and assigned ownership.

00:00:36.574 --> 00:00:43.462
Vulnerability teams can use observed reachability, asset function, and dependencies to improve prioritization.

00:00:43.462 --> 00:00:46.549
A useful investigation joins sources.

00:00:46.549 --> 00:00:55.337
A remote-access session, firewall connection, engineering-workstation logon, controller interaction, and historian trend may describe one operational story.

00:00:55.337 --> 00:01:00.799
Reliable time and consistent asset identifiers make that correlation possible.

00:01:00.799 --> 00:01:13.386
SOC alerts need OT context: site, zone, asset role, criticality, protocol or action, maintenance state, supporting evidence, and the team that can validate process meaning.

00:01:13.386 --> 00:01:20.749
Generic severity without this information shifts work to the analyst and increases unsafe assumptions.

00:01:20.749 --> 00:01:25.261
Escalation should connect security with operations and engineering.

00:01:25.261 --> 00:01:36.423
They can distinguish a cyber event from equipment failure, planned maintenance, or process transition and can advise which containment actions are safe.

00:01:36.423 --> 00:01:43.786
Automated isolation should be used cautiously where it could remove control, visibility, or redundancy.

00:01:43.786 --> 00:01:47.823
Every investigation should improve the telemetry program.

00:01:47.823 --> 00:01:55.185
Correct asset records, repair collection gaps, tune detections, preserve new indicators, and update runbooks.

00:01:55.185 --> 00:02:03.498
Telemetry creates value when it moves from collection to shared evidence, coordinated decisions, and measurable improvement.
